  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 126 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nMonday through Friday\n\nSoutherly winds will return quickly Monday ahead of another\napproaching low pressure trough. This should result in even\nmilder conditions, with high temps likely cracking at least 60\nmost places. Dry weather should persist, with the surface low \npassing well to the north again.\n\nA stronger upper level trough is expected to drop through the\nregion later next week. Current deterministic model runs \nsuggest this could be the coldest airmass of the season thus \nfar. GFS and ECMWF ensemble temp means also show this potential \nfor a shot of colder air. Shower chances would likely return \nThursday into Friday if this stronger trough does drop through \nthe area.\n\nDDV",
